Categorical Encoding

The Category variable is categorical and is converted into numerical values using LabelEncoder.

The trained encoder is saved so that the Streamlit application can transform new user inputs in the same way as the training data.

Model

The project uses XGBoost Regressor for demand prediction.

XGBoost is a gradient boosting algorithm based on decision trees. Multiple trees are built sequentially, with later trees improving upon the errors made by previous trees.

Hyperparameter Tuning

RandomizedSearchCV is used to search for a suitable combination of model hyperparameters.

The search space includes:

n_estimators
max_depth
learning_rate
subsample
colsample_bytree
min_child_weight

The model is evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE) during cross-validation.

Model Evaluation

The trained model is evaluated on the test dataset using:

MAE

Mean Absolute Error measures the average absolute difference between actual and predicted demand.

MSE

Mean Squared Error calculates the average squared prediction error.

RMSE

Root Mean Squared Error is the square root of MSE and expresses prediction error in the same units as demand.

R² Score

R² measures how much of the variation in demand is explained by the model.

